Witness of linux-ida-find-first-range (lib/idr.c, ida_find_first_range()).

  make LINUX=<kernel tree> harness   builds tools/testing/radix-tree once
  make LINUX=<kernel tree> run       exit 1 while the bug is there

Needs liburcu (URCU_PFX, default ~/.local/urcu_extract/usr).

Expected at v7.1 (8cd9520d35a6), checked 2026-11-07:
  ida_find_first_range(ida = {0, 1024}, 1, 2999) = -2 (want 1024)
  BUG: the search stopped at block 0
  exit 1

The repro is the write-up's own code.  hegel-c's pin
tests/irl/linux/pins/ida_find_first_range.conf runs a property test that
finds it without being told the input (shrinks to IDs {0, 1024}, range
(1, 1024)).
